#: applications/luci-app-wansentry/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wansentry/overview.js:381
msgid "Recommended. When an uplink changes state the kernel still holds conntrack entries pinned to the old gateway, and TCP treats the resulting ICMP unreachables as a soft error — so clients retransmit into a dead path for minutes instead of reconnecting. Flushing forces every connection to be re-established over the surviving uplink. The cost is that connections on the healthy uplink are dropped too, because mwan3's flush is global rather than per-uplink."
